---
const pageTitle = "Woujouh f Dhlem — JAPPER";
const pageDescription =
  "Presentation text for Woujouh f Dhlem, a work about darkness, the face, the opacity of the future, and expression outside the gaze.";

const shortText = [
  "Woujouh f Dhlem was born from a vision experienced in Tunis: that of an opaque black future for Tunisians living in Tunisia. A future with no visibility, no clear direction, no possibility of knowing how to move forward.",
  "From this vision, I wanted to create a physical situation close to this opacity. The participants were placed in total darkness, without light and without sound. They did not know they were going to be photographed, nor how long they would remain in that situation.",
  "The project seeks to capture a rare expression: that of a face that is neither looked at by others nor observed by itself. In total darkness, the face no longer responds to the external gaze and no longer composes itself in front of a mirror.",
  "Through these images, I seek to connect an experience born in Tunisia and in the Arab and Muslim world to a broader condition: finding oneself before a future with no visibility, no control, no clear direction. A human experience of uncertainty and opacity.",
];

const longSections = [
  {
    title: "1. The Initial Vision",
    paragraphs: [
      "The starting point of Woujouh f Dhlem is not a theoretical idea, but an event I actually experienced in Tunis.",
      "I was walking through a district of Tunis, near Jewish and Christian cemeteries. At that moment, with my eyes open, a vision appeared from within. The future of Tunisians living in Tunisia appeared to me as a black, opaque future.",
      "That vision was not a symbolic image created afterward. It appeared in my mind, in my head, in my body, as a physical sensation. What I saw was not simply a difficult future or a dark future, but a closed future, an unreadable future, a future with no visible depth and no clear direction.",
      "From this direct perception came the desire to give that vision a form, to make it visible, to make it physical, and to make it shareable with others.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "2. The Black Opaque Future",
    paragraphs: [
      "The expression that appeared in me was that of a black opaque future.",
      "It is not simply a dark future, a difficult future, or an uncertain future. A black opaque future is a future beyond which nothing can be seen. It becomes a closed surface without transparency, preventing every prediction and every projection.",
      "In such a situation, one does not know where to go, which direction to take, or even how to move forward. One does not even know whether moving forward is possible. From this impossibility of seeing ahead, the central question emerged: what feelings, what expressions appear on the faces of people placed before a completely opaque future?",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "3. Expression Outside the Gaze",
    paragraphs: [
      "Woujouh f Dhlem does not first aim to show faces. It asks what the expression of a face becomes when it escapes the gaze.",
      "In everyday life, the expressions of our faces are almost always affected by the gaze of others. When someone looks at us, our face changes. Even when we are not conscious of it, the feeling of being seen acts on our expression.",
      "There is another kind of expression, for example the expression that appears when we look at ourselves in front of a mirror. In that case, we are protected from an external gaze, but a gaze remains: our own gaze looking at ourselves. At that moment, the expression of the face changes through the act of observing oneself.",
      "What interests me here is a third state: the moment when no one is looking at us, and we are not looking at ourselves either. In complete darkness, there is neither an external gaze nor a gaze toward oneself. The face is not responding to anyone, and it is not shaping itself in front of a mirror.",
      "The question then becomes: in this situation, what expression appears on the face?",
      "What the work tries to capture is this rare, almost invisible expression. An expression born in complete darkness. A state in which the face exists, but is not being seen. Even we ourselves almost never have the opportunity to see the expression of our own face in complete darkness.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "4. The Method",
    paragraphs: [
      "To make this work, I tried to create a situation as close as possible to the idea of a black opaque future.",
      "The participants were placed in a space with no light at all and no sound at all. They did not know they were being photographed, and they did not know how long they would remain in that darkness. The aim was therefore not to ask them to pose, but to create physical conditions close to complete darkness.",
      "In that situation, the face no longer responds to the gaze of others, and the person can no longer see themself. The expression that appears there belongs to a very specific state: a moment without an external gaze, without a mirror, without visibility.",
      "Photography here attempts to connect two elements that contradict one another: human expression and the black opacity that would normally prevent that expression from being seen.",
      "The central question of this method can be stated as follows.",
    ],
    quote: "How can an expression be made to appear without erasing the darkness?",
  },
  {
    title: "5. Context and Sharing",
    paragraphs: [
      "This work is situated in the context of Tunisia after the 2011 revolution. That revolution ended more than twenty years of authoritarian rule. It was not led by a political party, by the army, or by a specific ideology. It emerged from a broad civic movement carried by people who wanted to end dictatorship, the suppression of freedom of expression, corruption, inequality, and social injustice.",
      "Compared with other processes involving the overthrow of power, this revolution was largely nonviolent. Violence did not come from the democratic movement itself, but from the regime that tried to suppress it. I consider this point important because it goes against several images of Arabs and Muslims that have become dominant today.",
      "At first, this revolution was widely praised, especially in Western countries, as a democratic and civic movement. It opened great hope not only in Tunisia, but also in several Arab and Muslim countries. It became the starting point of the Arab Spring, a series of movements against dictatorship and authoritarianism.",
      "Gradually, however, the external gaze changed. The media, especially Western media, which had initially praised this democratic rise, later focused heavily on instability, violence, and terrorism. Through this focus, civic movements, struggles for democracy, and people working for freedom in Arab and Muslim countries were often pushed into the background.",
      "This shift in discourse also reinforced images of Arabs and Muslims as dangerous and violent people. What I want to state here is that Arabs and Muslims are not more dangerous or more violent than other peoples, other civilizations, or other religions.",
      "This work takes shape in the gap between the initial democratic hope and the process through which the future gradually becomes dark and opaque. It begins from a vision experienced in Tunisia, but it also resonates with people in Arab and Muslim countries facing war, violence, crisis, and a future they can neither control nor foresee.",
      "Through these images, I try to connect a world that may seem distant from Japan with a situation many people can understand: being placed before a future without visibility, a future that cannot be controlled, a future without a clear direction. What begins in Tunisia and in the Arab and Muslim world can resonate elsewhere, not as a foreign reality, but as a human experience of uncertainty and opacity.",
    ],
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
  </head>

  <body class="woujouhPage">
    <nav class="woujouhNav" aria-label="Minimal navigation">
      <div class="woujouhNavGroup">
        <a href="/works">Works</a>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </div>
      <div class="woujouhNavGroup" aria-label="Languages">
        <a href="/woujouh">FR</a>
        <a href="/en/woujouh" aria-current="page">EN</a>
        <a href="/jp/woujouh">JP</a>
        <a href="/ar/woujouh">AR</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main class="woujouhMain">
      <header class="woujouhHero">
        <h1>
          <span lang="ar" dir="rtl">وجوه في الظلام</span>
          <span>Woujouh f Dhlem</span>
          <span lang="ja">暗闇の中の表情</span>
          <span>Faces in the Obscurity</span>
        </h1>
      </header>

      <section class="woujouhSection" aria-labelledby="short-text">
        <h2 id="short-text">Short Text</h2>
        <div class="woujouhText">
          {shortText.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="woujouhSection" aria-labelledby="long-text">
        <h2 id="long-text">Long Text</h2>
        {longSections.map((section) => (
          <article class="woujouhLongSection">
            <h3>{section.title}</h3>
            <div class="woujouhText">
              {section.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
              {section.quote && <blockquote>{section.quote}</blockquote>}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </section>
    </main>

    <style>
      :global(html) {
        background: #000;
      }

      :global(body.woujouhPage) {
        min-height: 100vh;
        margin: 0;
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(105, 13, 18, 0.2), transparent 34rem),
          linear-gradient(180deg, #050505 0%, #000 34rem, #020202 100%);
        color: #f3efe8;
        font-family: sans-serif;
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }

      .woujouhNav {
        position: fixed;
        top: 18px;
        right: 18px;
        z-index: 20;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        justify-content: flex-end;
        gap: 10px;
      }

      .woujouhNavGroup {
        display: flex;
        gap: 10px;
      }

      .woujouhNav a {
        color: #f3efe8;
        text-decoration: none;
        border: 1px solid rgba(243, 239, 232, 0.3);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 8px 13px;
        font-size: 13px;
        line-height: 1;
        background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.48);
      }

      .woujouhNav a:hover,
      .woujouhNav a:focus-visible,
      .woujouhNav a[aria-current="page"] {
        border-color: rgba(243, 239, 232, 0.75);
      }

      .woujouhMain {
        width: min(100% - 40px, 760px);
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 112px 0 96px;
      }

      .woujouhHero {
        padding: 72px 0 86px;
      }

      .woujouhHero h1 {
        display: grid;
        gap: 18px;
        margin: 0;
        max-width: 14ch;
        color: #fffaf2;
        font-size: clamp(42px, 11vw, 82px);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.02;
      }

      .woujouhHero h1 span {
        display: block;
      }

      .woujouhHero h1 span:first-child {
        color: #c94b4b;
      }

      .woujouhHero h1 span:not(:first-child) {
        color: rgba(243, 239, 232, 0.68);
        font-size: 0.44em;
        line-height: 1.25;
      }

      .woujouhSection {
        margin-top: 86px;
        padding-top: 42px;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(243, 239, 232, 0.14);
      }

      .woujouhSection h2 {
        margin: 0 0 32px;
        color: #c94b4b;
        font-size: 15px;
        font-weight: 400;
        letter-spacing: 0.13rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      .woujouhText {
        display: grid;
        gap: 28px;
      }

      .woujouhText p,
      .woujouhText blockquote {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: 66ch;
        color: rgba(243, 239, 232, 0.84);
        font-size: clamp(17px, 4vw, 20px);
        line-height: 1.84;
      }

      .woujouhText blockquote {
        padding: 22px 0 22px 24px;
        border-left: 2px solid #c94b4b;
        color: #fffaf2;
        font-size: clamp(19px, 4.4vw, 24px);
      }

      .woujouhLongSection {
        margin-top: 62px;
      }

      .woujouhLongSection h3 {
        margin: 0 0 22px;
        color: #fffaf2;
        font-size: clamp(24px, 7vw, 34px);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.2;
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .woujouhNav {
          top: 14px;
          right: 14px;
          left: 14px;
        }

        .woujouhMain {
          width: min(100% - 32px, 760px);
          padding: 86px 0 72px;
        }

        .woujouhHero {
          padding: 56px 0 66px;
        }

        .woujouhSection {
          margin-top: 68px;
          padding-top: 34px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
